{"seq":1,"mint":"C16","verb":"claim","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","approach":"split","literals":false,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"there is no prior behaviour a flag would preserve","clause_quoted":true,"facts":["F2"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"pub fn render_text(display_path: &str, items: &[BriefItem]) -> String {\n    let mut out = String::new();\n    out.push_str(&format!(\n        \"grounding brief: {display_path} — {} claim(s), scope withheld\\n\\n\",\n        items.len()\n    ));\n    for item in items {\n        out.push_str(&format!(\"id: {}\\n\", item.id));\n        out.push_str(&format!(\"proposition: {}\\n\", item.proposition));\n        if let Some(pin) = &item.pin {\n            out.push_str(&format!(\"pin: {pin}\\n\"));\n        }\n        out.push_str(\"scope: WITHHELD\\n\\n\");\n    }\n    out\n}","why":"The captured current renderer already defines prior brief behaviour: it emits the grounding brief with its existing fields and no owed section. An additive flag would have to preserve this existing no-owed output when not enabled, so the assertion that there is no prior behaviour to preserve is incompatible with the captured implementation.","quoted":true}],"at":1790113045,"cost":0.0120535,"elapsed_ms":83957,"attempts":3,"not_verbatim":0,"literals_refuted":0,"not_a_quantity":0,"kind_off_verb":0,"refuted":0}
